  "description": "Extracts α_shift(I; λ, μ, ν) per λ ⊢ 6 in the deuteron case (I = single inter-nucleon averaged crossing) via LR-system inversion. Runs 100 (β_1, β_2) Hecke-element test pairs to over-determine the α_shift unknowns per λ, then solves by least squares. For c^λ_{μν} = 1 cases, the scalar α_shift values are consistent with character data to ~1e-13 (machine precision). For c^λ_{μν} ≥ 2 cases (only λ = (3,2,1) for n=6), the formula is matrix-valued and requires the refined Sub-lemma 2.1 statement.",
